<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jean Joseph Amable Humbert</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1767">1767</a>–<a href="/years/1823">1823</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as General Humbert</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jean Joseph Amable Humbert was a French general of the Revolutionary Wars. In August 1798 he landed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/killala">Killala</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-mayo">County Mayo</a> with about a thousand troops to support the Irish rebellion and routed government forces at Castlebar, but he surrendered to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-cornwallis-1st-marquess-cornwallis">Lord Cornwallis</a> at Ballinamuck in September. He later settled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-orleans">New Orleans</a>, where he died.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jean-joseph-amable-humbert.jpg" alt="Jean Joseph Amable Humbert" width="320" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: François Bonneville · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:G%C3%A9n%C3%A9ral_Jean_Humbert.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
